Below is a prompt you can paste directly into Claude. It tells Claude to recreate the website almost pixel-perfect, while modernizing the code structure and adding a complete admin mode. It also forces everything into a single HTML file (HTML + CSS + JavaScript).

⸻

Prompt

You are a senior UI/UX designer and frontend engineer.

Your task is to recreate the website shown in the attached screenshot as accurately as possible.

The goal is NOT to redesign it. The goal is to faithfully recreate the original interface while using modern HTML/CSS/JavaScript.

Everything must be inside ONE SINGLE HTML FILE.

No frameworks.

No Bootstrap.

No React.

No Vue.

No external CSS.

No external JS.

Only plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript.

Use CSS variables.

Use Flexbox and Grid.

The page must be responsive while preserving the original desktop appearance.

⸻

General Appearance

The website is an old Israeli Air Force internal portal.

The design should intentionally preserve the early-2010s government/intranet aesthetic.

Do not modernize the colors.

Do not flatten the interface.

Keep gradients.

Keep borders.

Keep shadows.

Keep spacing.

Keep proportions.

Keep the original feeling.

